# Documentation synchronization (`.docs/`)

You are maintaining documentation for a **Next.js 16 App Router** MLS project. **`.docs/`** is the single source of truth for application flow, module behavior, file responsibility, and feature documentation—alongside:

| Top-level doc | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `.docs/application.md` | Whole-app reference (routes, auth, APIs, architecture) |
| `.docs/folder-structure.md` | Repository tree diagram (see `folder-structure-sync` rule) |
| `.docs/packages.md` | `package.json` dependencies (see `packages-docs-sync` rule) |

**Code changes are incomplete if `.docs` is not updated.** Documentation updates are mandatory; never skip them.

---

## 1. When to update

Whenever any **source** file or folder under `src/` or `app/` is **created, updated, renamed, moved, or deleted**, update the corresponding `.docs` markdown in the **same session**.

Also update `.docs/application.md` when behavior affects app-wide flows (routing, auth, APIs, profile menu, providers).

---

## 2. Mirror structure

Documentation paths mirror the repo, rooted under `.docs/`:

| Source | Documentation |
| --- | --- |
| `src/features/auth/components/SignInForm.tsx` | `.docs/src/features/auth/components/SignInForm.md` |
| `src/features/auth/components/` | `.docs/src/features/auth/components/README.md` |
| `app/[locale]/(main)/dashboard/page.tsx` | `.docs/app/[locale]/(main)/dashboard/page.md` |

Use the same folder names and file basename (`.md` instead of `.tsx`/`.ts`).

**Folder READMEs** are required for major areas, e.g.:

- `.docs/src/features/auth/README.md`
- `.docs/src/features/property/README.md`
- `.docs/src/components/ui/README.md`
- `.docs/src/apis/README.md`
- `.docs/src/providers/README.md`
- `.docs/app/[locale]/README.md`

---

## 3. Per-file markdown template

Each file-level `.md` must include **all sections that apply** (omit only if truly N/A):

### File Overview
- Purpose, where used, related feature/module

### Responsibilities
- Main duties, business logic, UI behavior

### Imports
- Important modules, services, hooks, components

### Exports
- Functions, components, types

### State Management
- Zustand, React Query, local state

### API Usage
- APIs, mutations/queries, endpoints

### Navigation
- Routes, locale-prefixed URLs, `useRouter` / `Link` from `@/src/i18n/navigation`

### Props / Parameters
- Props, hook params, function arguments

### Actions / Inputs
- Enumerate user inputs controlled by the UI (form fields, toggle state, checkbox values, etc.)
- Enumerate user actions/events (submit, open modal views, navigation clicks, logout confirmation, etc.)
- If there are show/hide toggles (e.g. password visibility), declare them and explain what state they toggle.
- If inputs have validation, list what validations can fail (required/format/length) and the error message keys used.

### UI Details
- Tailwind, **semantic tokens** (`bg-page`, `text-muted`, etc.)
- `rounded-xl` (cards/modals/popovers) vs `rounded-lg` (controls)
- Light/dark theme, responsive/mobile-first, a11y

### Flow Description
- Step-by-step flow, user interactions, data flow, loading/error/success

### Dependencies
- Related files, parent/child relationships

### Notes
- Edge cases, TODOs, limitations

Use headings, tables, code blocks, and bullet lists. Be **detailed, technical, and beginner-friendly**. Explain **why** the file exists, **how** it works, **where** it connects—never vague one-liners.

---

## 4. Folder README template

Each major folder `README.md` must cover:

- Purpose and architecture of the folder
- Flow between files and dependency relationships
- Conventions and feature lifecycle
- Routing behavior (if applicable)
- API interaction flow (if applicable)

---

## 5. Architecture context

Document against the real stack:

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19
- **next-intl** (`localePrefix: always` — routes like `/en/listing`)
- TanStack Query, Zustand, Axios (`authClient` / `apiClient`)
- Tailwind CSS v4, Headless UI
- Feature-first layout under `src/features/<name>/`

---

## 6. Locale-aware navigation

When documenting navigation:

- Always show **locale-prefixed** examples (`/en/my-profile`, not only `/my-profile`)
- Prefer `useRouter`, `Link`, `redirect` from `@/src/i18n/navigation`
- Note `NavigationInitializer` + `navigation.utils` for imperative redirects (e.g. logout, 401)

---

## 7. Styling in docs

- Document **semantic tokens** only; do not recommend raw `gray-*` / hex for themed UI
- Reference light/dark via `ThemeProvider` and `globals.css` variables
- Mobile-first responsive patterns (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`)

---

## 8. Auth-related files

Always document when relevant:

- Query params: `auth`, `from`, `otp-flow`, OTP contact keys (`authViews.ts`)
- `AuthModal` view switching and `AUTH_VIEW` constants
- Token storage (`token.store`), `AuthProvider`, `auth.store`
- Mutation lifecycle (`auth.mutation.ts`), logout redirect behavior

---

## 9. API / service files

Include:

- Endpoint path and HTTP method
- Auth required (`auth: true` on client)
- Request/response shapes (point to `*.types.ts`)
- Interceptors, 401 refresh, redirect on failure

---

## 10. Change tracking

On code changes, update docs for:

- Flow descriptions, imports/exports, routes, dependency graphs
- **Rename** `.md` files when source files rename
- **Delete** obsolete `.md` and fix parent README links

Docs must reflect the **current** codebase only.

---

## 11. New files and folders

| Action | Documentation action |
| --- | --- |
| New source file | Create matching `.docs/.../*.md` with full template |
| New source folder | Create folder `README.md` + child docs as files appear |
| Delete source | Remove mirrored `.md`; update parent READMEs |
| Move/rename source | Move/rename mirrored `.md`; update references |

---

## 12. Exclusions

- Do **not** mirror documentation for paths excluded from `folder-structure.md` tree **unless** they are intentional doc targets (e.g. updating `.docs/application.md` itself).
- Changes **only** under `.cursor/`, `.git/`, `.next/`, `node_modules/`, etc. do not require new mirrored `src/` docs.
- Editing `.docs/packages.md` or `.docs/folder-structure.md` follows their dedicated rules, not per-file mirroring.

---

## 13. Workflow (same session)

1. Implement code change under `src/` or `app/`.
2. Create/update/delete mirrored `.docs/...` files and folder READMEs.
3. Update `.docs/application.md` if routes, auth, APIs, or global flows changed.
4. Update `.docs/folder-structure.md` if the on-disk tree changed (non-excluded paths).
5. Update `.docs/packages.md` if `package.json` dependencies changed.

**Bulk scaffold:** `node scripts/bootstrap-docs.mjs` — then review and enrich critical flows (auth, navigation, layouts); do not treat generated text as final without verification.

## 14. Quality bar

Documentation consistency is **mandatory**. Prefer updating existing docs over adding duplicate summaries. Keep `.docs/application.md` as the index-level overview; use mirrored files for file-level depth. Doc index: `.docs/README.md`.
